# Add Delete Student Feature in Admin Panel

This plan outlines the steps to add a "Delete Student" feature to the Admin panel's Student Tracking table. 

## Proposed Changes

We need to add a secure way for administrators to delete a student's account entirely. Deleting a user from Supabase's Auth system (`auth.users`) will trigger our database constraints (`ON DELETE CASCADE`) to automatically delete their profile, submissions, badges, and xp logs cleanly.

### 1. Server Action
#### [NEW] `src/features/admin/actions/adminActions.ts` (or add to an existing file)
- Create an `async function deleteStudent(studentId: string)` server action.
- This action will initialize a Supabase client using the `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`. (Standard server clients don't have permission to delete users from the authentication table; the service role key bypasses RLS and allows admin-level auth modifications).
- It will call `supabase.auth.admin.deleteUser(studentId)`.

### 2. UI Updates
#### [NEW] `src/app/(admin)/admin/students/components/DeleteStudentButton.tsx`
- Create a client component that contains a "Delete" button.
- When clicked, it will prompt the admin with a standard browser `window.confirm("Are you sure you want to delete this student? This action cannot be undone.")` to prevent accidental deletions.
- If confirmed, it calls the `deleteStudent` server action and triggers a router refresh to update the table.

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(admin)/admin/students/page.tsx`
- Add a new "Actions" column to the `<th>` of the students table.
- Add a corresponding `<td>` in the row mapping that renders the `<DeleteStudentButton studentId={student.id} />`.

